{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://schemas.traigent.ai/analytics/pareto_problem_schema.json",
  "title": "Run Pareto Problem",
  "description": "Closed RFC 9457 problem documents of experiment_run.get_run_pareto (application/problem+json). Each definition is one status/code/type combination of the backend problem catalogue (src/api_kit/problems.py PROBLEMS) with its fixed title, detail and server-minted problem_id (first 32 hex of sha256 of the type URN); nothing the client sent is echoed. NotFoundProblem is the one closed 404 for a missing, foreign, ungranted, revoked or retired run: identical bytes in every case. BadRequestProblem is a malformed experiment_run_ref, an out-of-range limit or request_count, an x_measure or y_measure containing control characters, or an unknown or retired query parameter (page, offset and every undeclared name); it never echoes the offending value (syntax is validated before any lookup). ServiceUnavailableProblem is the declared outcome when the Pareto analysis cannot be produced within its budget (serialized response over 1 MiB, more than 10000 scoped configuration rows, counted before any metric processing, deadline exhausted, a configuration whose trial_ref is not yet issued, or a required dependency down): the response is refused, never a partial analysis presented as complete. 429 and 503 may carry a Retry-After header. InvalidCursorProblem (backend src/api_kit/problems.py:33, code invalid_cursor, 400) is any invalid or stale cursor: malformed or over-long, not belonging to this caller, project, run and query, or whose analysis_revision no longer matches the run; it echoes nothing. ServiceUnavailableProblem is also the outcome when a stored metric name is outside the shared name class (control characters, empty or over 100 characters): never truncated or sanitized.",
